    "content": "<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/DCD301/flm1/d01/001.webp\" alt=\"DCD301 · Chapter 0 COURSE INTRODUCATION · slide 1: Digital Design\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Chapter 0 COURSE INTRODUCATION · slide 1/9</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Digital Design<br>Digital Design. M. Morris Mano , and Michael D. Ciletti. Pearson, Sixth edition, 2013<br>COURSE INTRODUCATION</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/DCD301/flm1/d01/002.webp\" alt=\"DCD301 · Chapter 0 COURSE INTRODUCATION · slide 2: Syllabus Details\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Chapter 0 COURSE INTRODUCATION · slide 2/9</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Syllabus Details<br>Description<br>Study hour (150h) = 45h contact hours + 1h final exam + 104h self-stud<br>This course provides students with a solid and comprehensive foundation in digital circuit design. It begins with essential concepts such as number systems, logic gates, Boolean algebra, and logic function simplification.<br>Students then advance to designing and implementing combinational and sequential logic circuits, including multiplexers, arithmetic circuits, flip-flops, shift registers, counters, and memory elements.</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/DCD301/flm1/d01/003.webp\" alt=\"DCD301 · Chapter 0 COURSE INTRODUCATION · slide 3: Syllabus Details\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Chapter 0 COURSE INTRODUCATION · slide 3/9</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Syllabus Details<br>Description<br>The course also introduces hardware description languages (VHDL/Verilog), FPGA - based implementation, and fundamental principles of digital signal and data processing. Through these topics, students learn how hardware is described at the Register - Transfer Level (RTL) and how it is verified using testbenches and simulation.</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/DCD301/flm1/d01/004.webp\" alt=\"DCD301 · Chapter 0 COURSE INTRODUCATION · slide 4: Syllabus Details\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Chapter 0 COURSE INTRODUCATION · slide 4/9</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Syllabus Details<br>Description<br>In addition, the course provides an overview of the Digital IC Design Flow, including:<br>Specification and Functional Requirements<br>RTL Design using HDL<br>Functional Verification and Testbench DevelopmentLogic Synthesis to Gate-Level Netlist<br>Timing Analysis and Optimization<br>Implementation on FPGA or placement &amp; routing (for ASIC).<br>Post-synthesis simulation and sign - off checks</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/DCD301/flm1/d01/005.webp\" alt=\"DCD301 · Chapter 0 COURSE INTRODUCATION · slide 5: Syllabus Details\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Chapter 0 COURSE INTRODUCATION · slide 5/9</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Syllabus Details<br>Description<br>The module emphasizes not only technical competence but also professional ethics, social responsibility, and the development of creativity and problem - solving skills.<br>Students apply theoretical knowledge through laboratory exercises, hands - on projects, and real-world design practices.&quot;</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/DCD301/flm1/d01/006.webp\" alt=\"DCD301 · Chapter 0 COURSE INTRODUCATION · slide 6: Syllabus Details\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Chapter 0 COURSE INTRODUCATION · slide 6/9</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Syllabus Details<br>Student Tasks<br>Students must attend at least 80% of contact sessions in order to be accepted to the final examination.<br>Student is responsible to do all exercises given by instructor in class or at home and submit on time.<br>Use laptop in class only for learning purpose<br>Promptly access to the https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/ for up-to-date course information.</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/DCD301/flm1/d01/007.webp\" alt=\"DCD301 · Chapter 0 COURSE INTRODUCATION · slide 7: Syllabus Details\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Chapter 0 COURSE INTRODUCATION · slide 7/9</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Syllabus Details<br>Intenet<br>Textbook<br>Design and Simulator software (Cedance, https://www.edaplayground.com, Xilinx, …)<br>Tools<br>Course component grades<br>1. On-ging Assessment:<br>2 Progress Tests\t: 20%<br>2 Assignments\t: 10%<br>3 Lab\t\t: 30%<br>2. Final Exam\t: 40%<br>3. Final result\t: 100%<br>4. Completion criteria:<br>Progress Tests &gt; 0<br>Labs &gt; 0<br>Final Exam score &gt;=4 &amp; Final Result &gt;=5</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/DCD301/flm1/d01/008.webp\" alt=\"DCD301 · Chapter 0 COURSE INTRODUCATION · slide 8: Syllabus Details\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Chapter 0 COURSE INTRODUCATION · slide 8/9</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Syllabus Details<br>Topic &amp; Session<br>Chapter 1: Digital Systems and Binary Numbers<br>Chapter 2:  Boolean Algebra and logic Gates<br>Chapter 3: Gate-Level Minimization(cont)<br>Progress Test 1 (Ch.1–3)<br>Lab1: Digital Logic Fundamentals<br>Chapter 4: Combinational logic<br>Chapter 5: Synchronous Sequential Logic<br>Assignment 1</p></div>\n<div class=\"anh-slide\"><img src=\"https://media.cuongthai.com/images/academy/DCD301/flm1/d01/009.webp\" alt=\"DCD301 · Chapter 0 COURSE INTRODUCATION · slide 9: Syllabus Details\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1280\" height=\"720\" /><p class=\"chu-thich\">Chapter 0 COURSE INTRODUCATION · slide 9/9</p></div>\n<div class=\"trich-slide\"><p class=\"nhan\">Trên slide · On the slide</p><p>Syllabus Details<br>Topic &amp; Session<br>Chapter 6: Registers and Counters<br>Chapter 7: Memory and Programmable logic<br>Chapter 8: Design at the Register<br>Chapter 9:  Asynchronous Sequential logic<br>Assignment 2<br>Chapter 10: Digital Integrated Circuits<br>Lab 2: Digital Circuit Design using SystemVerilog &amp; EDAPlayground<br>Lab 3: XOR Gate Design (Digital Design)<br>Progress Test 2 (Ch.4–8)</p></div>"
